 &lt;figcaption id="caption-265d8b771b2f5102a0c5418447cfb019"&gt;
 My old sharp MZ-800, needing some brush up. On top the original
floppy cable and parts of the MZ-1F19 floppy disk drive, as well as a
shugart-adapter. The original case of the MZ-1F19 was misused in the 90ies to
host a CD writer an is now lost.
 &lt;/figcaption&gt;
&lt;/figure&gt;

&lt;p&gt;After the Atari 600XL, the Sharp MZ-800 was my second computer, back in the
80ies. Since I still had the computer and a box of more 35 year old 5.25&amp;quot;
floppy disks, I was curious to see my early works as a teen aged programmer.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>